                 |CKBChapter 6 - Healing, Food and Drink
                 |BKB-----------------------------------

|YKOYour hit points and spell points recover naturally when you stop fighting.
Use |YKBsit|YKO while you wait in a safe room. Food, drink, potions, guild
abilities, and other effects can restore resources faster.

Pubs and inns sell healing fare. Read |YKBmenu|YKO, use
|YKBmenu usable|YKO when it is available, then
|YKBbuy <number>|YKO or |YKBorder <number>|YKO. An item may restore HP, SP,
or both, and stronger fare is intended for stronger characters. Carry a few
emergency supplies before leaving town, but remember that food and drink do
not belong to the saved-gear system.

Use |YKBbuffs|YKO to review active buffs and debuffs. Read item
descriptions before consuming anything: not every effect is beneficial, and
some healing methods belong to a particular guild, class, or location.

Corpses can also become a small source of income. An ash processor can provide
a corpse burner. Carry it, use |YKBburn corpse|YKO after a fight, inspect its
contents with |YKBcheck burner|YKO, and return to a processor to
|YKBprocess all ash|YKO. |YKBset autoburn on|YKO automates the burn only
after other corpse processing; anything left in the corpse is destroyed.

At low health, retreat first and recover second. A meal is not a substitute
for |YKBwimpy|YKO, an escape route, or help from another player.|000

